# Answer key for B8 t3_interaction.sql - procedural PL/pgSQL, interaction.
#
# WRITTEN FROM SOURCE BEFORE THE ANALYSER WAS RUN OVER THIS FILE.
# Conventions: all earlier decisions, OBJECTIVES.md rules 1-9, D-39..D-42 (decided
# 2026-10-04, not implemented). Variables are `var:<name>`; bands per edge (rule 5): the
# hardest construct on the edge's path decides.

@ 20 S1 constant dynamic SQL in a loop
origin mart.fn_loop_dyn 2
value staging.customers.segment -> mart.kpi_rollup.segment identity
filter staging.orders.status -> mart.kpi_rollup
note The loop query's WHERE decides which passes run (rule 4); the write is dynamic, so band 2. rd.channel arrives by USING: an external value (D-42), no edge.

@ 33 S2 the scalar function's SELECT INTO
origin mart.fn_store_region 1
value core.dim_store.region -> var:mart.fn_store_region.v_region identity
filter core.dim_store.id -> core.dim_store
filter var:mart.fn_store_region.p_store -> core.dim_store

@ 44 S3 the trigger body
origin mart.trg_big_order 2
value staging.orders.channel -> mart.channel_mix.channel identity
value core.dim_store.region -> mart.channel_mix.region identity
value staging.orders.amount -> mart.channel_mix.revenue identity
filter staging.orders.amount -> mart.channel_mix
note The WHEN (NEW.amount > 1000) decides whether the body runs (D-41). fn_store_region contributes s.region (rule 6).
forbid value staging.orders.store_id -> mart.channel_mix.region identity | NEW.store_id is only the function's argument

@ 68 S4 a RETURN QUERY function read under GROUP BY
value staging.order_lines.product_id -> mart.product_performance.product_id identity
value staging.order_lines.quantity -> mart.product_performance.units aggregated
value staging.order_lines.quantity, staging.order_lines.unit_price -> mart.product_performance.revenue aggregated
influence staging.order_lines.product_id -> mart.product_performance.units, mart.product_performance.revenue
filter staging.order_lines.status -> mart.product_performance

@ 83 S5 a loop over a RETURN QUERY function
origin mart.fn_loop_over_fn 1
value staging.order_lines.unit_price -> core.dim_product.list_price identity
filter staging.order_lines.status, staging.order_lines.product_id, core.dim_product.product_id -> core.dim_product
note Function inlined in the loop query (D-40), its WHERE carried into the body (rule 4); rf.pid is ol.product_id.

@ 99 S6 the threshold
origin mart.fn_threshold_loop 1
value staging.payments.amount -> var:mart.fn_threshold_loop.v_avg aggregated

@ 103 S7 in the loop: variable in WHERE, record in SET
origin mart.fn_threshold_loop 1
value core.dim_warehouse.capacity -> mart.carrier_scorecard.shipments identity
filter core.dim_warehouse.id, mart.carrier_scorecard.carrier_id, mart.carrier_scorecard.cost_per_kg, var:mart.fn_threshold_loop.v_avg -> mart.carrier_scorecard
